<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32918" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">orchēstra</span></b> , ae,
		f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρχήστρα</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The place where the Senate sat</i> in the theatre,
				<i>the orchestra</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in orchestrā senatorum sunt sedibus
					loca destinata,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr. 5,
					6</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Juv. 7, 47</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Caes. 39</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Aug. 35</span></i>; <i><span class="en">44</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id.
				Claud. 21</span></i> et saep.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>the Senate</i>
				(<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">similesque videbis Orchestram et populum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					3, 178</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Another place on the stage</i>, acc. to <i><span class="en">Fest. p.
				181</span></i> b; cf. Müll. ad h. l.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
